  "notes": "Public Law 20-48 requires school from 5 to 17, so kindergarten is compulsory; a child must be 5 by September 30 to enter it. Kindergarten is still left out, as in the US file, so Grade 1 starts at 6. CNMI PSS counts its middle schools as grades 6–8 and high schools as 9–12, so elementary schools end at grade 5; the junior/senior high schools on Rota and Tinian teach grades 6–12 together. Freshman to senior for grades 9–12 is everyday US usage, not from the cited pages."
